module bankr-ohn-local-rules.local-rules

import core.frbp9006.{ frbp9006 }
import frbp.events.{ PetitionFiled }

// The Bankr. N.D. Ohio court's own periods and page limit, counted under
// FRBP 9006(a), the FRCP 6(a) method: the Local Bankruptcy Rules as last
// revised May 19, 2022. The FRBP periods (schedules, claims, the chapter 13
// plan, discharge, dischargeability, exemptions, the adversary answer,
// appeals) are lit/frbp's and are not declared again. The motion response
// period of LBR 9013-1(a)-(b) is 14 days unless an FRBP, a statute or the
// court sets another time; it is declared at 14 days and yields to those.
// Stated in the rules but not declared: the certification of plan votes,
// due 'prior to or at' the confirmation hearing (LBR 3018-2), which has no
// counted period.
/// A motion or a response to it, including written argument and cited
/// authorities, exclusive of appendices and attached unreported opinions
/// (LBR 9013-2(a), (d)).
limit motion-paper { pages <= 20 cite "N.D. Ohio LBR 9013-2(a)" } cite "N.D. Ohio LBR 9013-2(a)"

/// A trial or hearing on any matter is scheduled to be held (LBR
/// 2091-1(c)).
event TrialOrHearingScheduled()
/// The discovery cut-off passes (LBR 7026-1).
event DiscoveryCutoff()
/// A motion or application is served, as shown on its certificate of
/// service (LBR 9013-1(a)-(b)).
event MotionServed()
/// A response to a motion or application is served, as shown on its
/// certificate of service (LBR 9013-1(c)).
event ResponseServed()
/// The final pretrial is scheduled to be held (LBR 9070-1(a)(6)).
event FinalPretrialScheduled()
/// Final judgment, or final judgment on appeal, is entered (LBR
/// 9070-1(b)(2)).
event FinalJudgmentEntered()
/// A motion or response to a motion is filed (LBR 9013-2(a)).
event MotionPaperFiled() paper motion-paper

/// LBR 2016-2(c): a bankruptcy petition preparer seeking a determination
/// that its services are worth more than the presumptive $125 files a
/// motion requesting a hearing within 14 days after the petition is filed.
deadline preparer-fee-motion-period: 14.days after PetitionFiled() counted_by frbp9006 cite "N.D. Ohio LBR 2016-2(c)"

/// LBR 2091-1(c): unless otherwise ordered, an attorney of record may not
/// withdraw within 21 days before a trial or hearing on any matter.
deadline attorney-withdrawal-period: 21.days before TrialOrHearingScheduled() counted_by frbp9006 cite "N.D. Ohio LBR 2091-1(c)"

/// LBR 7026-1: unless otherwise ordered, no discovery dispute may be
/// brought to a judge, and no motion to compel filed, more than 14 days
/// after the discovery cut-off.
deadline discovery-dispute-period: 14.days after DiscoveryCutoff() counted_by frbp9006 cite "N.D. Ohio LBR 7026-1"

/// LBR 9013-1(a)-(b): unless the court orders otherwise, a response
/// opposing a motion or application is filed within 14 days (or such other
/// time as an FRBP, a statute or the court sets) from the date of service
/// on the certificate of service, subject to FRBP 9006(f).
deadline motion-response-period: 14.days after MotionServed() counted_by frbp9006 cite "N.D. Ohio LBR 9013-1(b)"

/// LBR 9013-1(c): subject to FRBP 9006(f), a reply may be filed within 7
/// days after the date of service of the response.
deadline motion-reply-period: 7.days after ResponseServed() counted_by frbp9006 cite "N.D. Ohio LBR 9013-1(c)"

/// LBR 9070-1(a)(6): unless otherwise ordered, the index of trial exhibits
/// is filed and served no later than 7 days before the final pretrial.
deadline exhibit-index-period: 7.days before FinalPretrialScheduled() counted_by frbp9006 cite "N.D. Ohio LBR 9070-1(a)"

/// LBR 9070-1(b)(2): counsel removes an exhibit held by the Clerk within 60
/// days after final judgment or final judgment on appeal; the Clerk
/// disposes of exhibits not removed.
deadline exhibit-removal-period: 60.days after FinalJudgmentEntered() counted_by frbp9006 cite "N.D. Ohio LBR 9070-1(b)"
